    {
      "text": "abide till ye go thence, Matt. 10:11 (Mark 6:10; Luke 9:4). Mary abode with her about three months, Luke 1:56. Zacchæus, … to day I must abide at thy house, Luke 19:5. Spirit descending … like a dove … abode upon him, John 1:32. They came … and abode with him that day, John 1:39. another Comforter, that he may abide with you, John 14:16. Abide in me, and I in you … except ye abide in me, John 15:4. If any man’s work abide … he shall receive a reward, 1 Cor. 3:14. wherein he is called, therein abide with God, 1 Cor. 7:24. now abideth faith, hope, charity, 1 Cor. 13:13. to abide in the flesh is more needful for you, Philip. 1:24. He that saith he abideth in him … walk … as he walked, 1 Jn. 2:6. are strong, and the word of God abideth in you, 1 Jn. 2:14. he that doeth the will of God abideth for ever, 1 Jn. 2:17. little children, abide in him, 1 Jn. 2:28. Whosoever abideth in him sinneth not, 1 Jn. 3:6. hereby we know that he abideth in us, 1 Jn. 3:24.",
